  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minnesota received $58.1M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,537 awards with an average award size of $37.8K. Minnesota's federal contract obligations fell 97.3% year over year. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Historical context shows much larger annual totals in prior years: FY22 totaled $2.5B, FY23 totaled $2.8B, FY24 totaled $3.3B, FY25 totaled $2.8B, and FY26 totaled $2.2B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date with $29.9M obligated, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $12M and the Department of Justice with $8.6M. ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC and NORTH STAR IMPORTS, LLC are the top vendors so far with $3.6M each, and MAYO CLINIC follows with $3.4M. Cheese Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $6.1M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $4.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to federal contracting in Minnesota this year?",
        "body": "Minnesota's federal contract obligations fell 97.3% year over year. Minnesota received $58.1M in FY2027 to date compared with multibillion-dollar totals in earlier fiscal years, including $2.2B in FY26 and $3.3B in FY24. The state recorded 1,537 awards so far with an average award size of $37.8K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and sellers so far in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $29.9M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $12M, and the Department of Justice obligated $8.6M. ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC and NORTH STAR IMPORTS, LLC each received $3.6M, and MAYO CLINIC received $3.4M. Cheese Manufacturing leads industries with $6.1M in obligations, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $4.1M."
      }
    ]
